  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Lokesh Kumar vs State on 3 October, 2017",
    "facts": "Petitioner has preferred this misc. petition under Section 482 of Cr.P.C. for quashing of FIR No.292/2017 of Police Station Sumerpur, Distt. Pali, for the offences under Sections 420, 486, 487, 272, 273 of IPC and Section 3 (1) (Z, Z) (11) Food Safety and Standard Act 2006. 2. On the basis of aforementioned information ASI of P.S. Sumerpur reached the shop and seized 16 Carton Oil (2 of 2) [CRLMP-3271/2017] under Section 102 of Cr.P.C. and the sample was taken and sent for FSL and the FSL report was received on 11.07.2016, on the basis of FSL report, present FIR has been filed.",
    "arguments": "At the outset, counsel for the petitioner submits that on the bare reading of the FIR, there is no allegation against the present petitioner as he is neither the owner of the adulterated mustard oil nor the shop in question nor the transport in question and therefore, prima facie no case has been made out against him on the bare reading of the FIR. 3. The facts of the case as noticed by this Court are that ASI P.S. Sumerpur on 27.02.2016 at 11.15 P.M. receiving information pertaining to some person storing adulterated mustard oil in the shop of New Rajendra Transport at Rajendra Market, Sumerpur. 4. Learned counsel for the petitioner further submits that the petitioner wants to submit a representation alongwith all the relevant documents before the concerned investigating authority.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "At the outset, counsel for the petitioner submits that on the bare reading of the FIR, there is no allegation against the present petitioner as he is neither the owner of the adulterated mustard oil nor the shop in question nor the transport in question and therefore, prima facie no case has been made out against him on the bare reading of the FIR. 3. The facts of the case as noticed by this Court are that ASI P.S. Sumerpur on 27.02.2016 at 11.15 P.M. receiving information pertaining to some person storing adulterated mustard oil in the shop of New Rajendra Transport at Rajendra Market, Sumerpur.",
    "respondent_arguments": "4. Learned counsel for the petitioner further submits that the petitioner wants to submit a representation alongwith all the relevant documents before the concerned investigating authority.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
